### Third-Party Notices & Attributions

This project includes algorithms, shader models, and runtime templates derived from or inspired by the following open-source projects:

1. **Libretro GLSL Shaders**
   - Source: https://github.com/libretro/glsl-shaders
   - The WebGL shader presets implemented in `tools/libretro-pipeline.js` and `tools/wasm_shell.html` are WebGL GLSL ports derived from the Libretro shader collection created by the Libretro community.
   - Individual shader algorithms and presets are credited to their respective authors:
     - `crt-consumer-light`: DariusG
     - `crt-geom-glow`: cgwg, hunterk
     - `fakelottes-ntsc-composite`: Timothy Lottes, leileilol, aliaspider
     - `crt-guest-dr-venom-kurozumi`: guest.r, Kurozumi
     - `retro-v2`: Hyllian
     - `color-mangler` / handheld color matrices: hunterk, Pokefan531
     - `c64-monitor-fast`: hunterk, torridgristle
     - `vector-glow`: aliaspider, hunterk
     - `scalefx`: Sp00kyFox

2. **Emscripten**
   - Source: https://github.com/emscripten-core/emscripten
   - Shell templates and WebAssembly runtime integration patterns are modeled after the Emscripten toolchain (University of Illinois / NCSA Open Source License and MIT License).
